          "section": "4. Discussion",
          "quote": "A decrease in grain size for low solution treatment temperature shows an increase in number of grain boundaries compared to high solution treatment temperature. Grain boundaries usually act as a strong obstacle to the transmission of slip from one crystal to its neighbor during deformation, which results in an increase in the yield strength and tensile strength.",
